cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "empirica-networks: online network experiments with Empirica"
message: >-
  If you use this software in research, please cite it. A methods paper is in
  preparation; until it exists, cite the software.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Feltham
    given-names: Eric Martin
    email: eric.feltham@aya.yale.edu
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8080-7119"
repository-code: "https://github.com/emfeltham/empirica-networks"
abstract: >-
  Network experiments for Empirica. Each participant has a private channel and
  receives only the projected state of their neighbors, so adjacency governs
  delivery rather than display. Includes fourteen topology generators with
  recorded seeds, rewiring during a session, neighbor-scoped messaging, and
  export helpers that record the realized graph rather than the generator's
  parameters. An evaluation command runs complete simulated sessions of a
  reconstructed published design and audits the delivered views afterwards.
keywords:
  - empirica
  - network experiments
  - social networks
  - behavioral experiments
  - experimental design
license: MIT
version: 0.0.0
